Q1 2026 (n3.d2, n3.d3). Shipments trail orders by about two quarters, so industry volume is weakening heading into 2027.\n- **Voltaris revenue run-rate:** Quarterly revenue was C$905M, 960M, 980M and 890M from 2025Q3 to 2026Q2 (n2.d3). That sums to about C$3.74B over the last four quarters. Q2 2026 fell about 9% from Q1.\n- **Gap to guidance:** C$4.2B needs about 12.5% growth over that trailing total. It also needs an average of C$1.05B a quarter, against C$890M in the latest quarter. With industry volume shrinking, that growth would have to come from share gains or price.\n- **Market share:** I could not find the CEA maker table, which the CEA report says holds each maker's figures. I therefore have no Voltaris share figure and cannot test the share-gain case directly.\n- **Offsetting evidence:** Voltaris reported H1 2026 orders up 11% year on year (n2.d2), which is the main support for growth. Even if orders carry through to revenue, 11% growth on the C$3.74B base gives about C$4.15B. That is just under guidance and assumes no industry drag.\n\n**Estimate:** Industry-implied 2027 revenue is roughly C$3.7–4.1B. The low end is flat on the trailing total, and the high end is orders-led growth of up to about 10%. C$4.2B would need Voltaris to clearly outgrow a shrinking market.","ttft_ms":2941,"type":"result","duration_ms":26987,"uuid":"f704d632-fa1b-46c4-aef3-3946b0d7a758","ttft_stream_ms":2229,"time_to_request_ms":69,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":5,"system_prompt":4,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":2,"input_attachments":8,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":2,"tool_pool_refresh":2,"init_message":8,"init_frame_send":2,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":5,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":1,"request_announcements":6,"query_setup":1,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":3,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":6,"request_build":6},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":